"""Blog / guides content — the only place article text lives.

Posts are plain data: no HTML, no templates, no Markdown parser. Each section
is a (kind, payload) tuple rendered by blog_post.html; kinds are:

  ("h2", text)                        section heading
  ("h3", text)                        sub-heading
  ("p",  text)                        paragraph
  ("ul", [item, ...])                 bullet list
  ("ol", [item, ...])                 numbered list
  ("cta", title, body, label, link)   call-to-action box; link is a
                                      ("panel", endpoint) or ("site", endpoint)
                                      pair rendered through panel_url/site_url

Keeping links out of the paragraph text means a renamed route or host can
never be stranded in an article — the template resolves every link.

Every article is about ENDHOST as a product: the app-hosting runtimes and the
deploy panel, the status engine and its embed builder, the free model. No
generic Minecraft content and no generic programming tutorials that drift off
the site's niche — the blog exists to explain the service to AdSense reviewers
and to users deciding whether to sign up.

POSTS stays in chronological order because that is how it reads and how it is
appended to; all_posts reverses it for display.
"""

